  "body": "Backend for turning **Configure Claude Code** from a two-key connect screen into a real settings editor. No UI yet — the page lands in the next PR.\n\n## What it does\n\nBuilt on the generated catalog from #114, so the editable surface tracks upstream instead of drifting: **518 entries**, each carrying the control it wants (`toggle`, `select` + option list, `number`, `path`, `list`, `JSON`, `secret`).\n\n| Route | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `GET /admin/api/claude-config/catalog` | what Claude Code can be configured to do |\n| `GET /admin/api/claude-config/document` | what this machine's settings file says |\n| `POST /admin/api/claude-config/plan` | what a set of edits *would* change |\n| `POST /admin/api/claude-config/apply` | make those edits |\n\n## The three traps, enforced in code\n\nA naive editor does the **opposite** of what the user asked on these, so they're handled server-side rather than left to the UI:\n\n- **Six presence-read variables.** Writing `\"0\"` to `DISABLE_TELEMETRY` leaves telemetry *off*. A request to set one falsey is **rewritten into a key removal**, with a warning explaining why.\n- **`FORCE_HYPERLINK` is parsed as a number**, so `\"false\"` enables hyperlinks. Setting it to a word is **rejected**, pointing at `0`.\n- **Ten credential variables** are masked on the way out.\n\n## Write safety\n\nTwo-stage. `plan_changes` touches no disk — resolves each request against the catalog, records `before`/`after`, attaches warnings. `apply_plan` writes only what the plan said, **after re-reading the file**: a plan the user reviewed for a minute must not clobber an edit made meanwhile. Backup taken once, atomic `os.replace`.\n\nTwo smaller correctness points, both with tests that fail without them:\n- Unsetting the last key under `permissions` **removes the empty parent** — Claude Code treats `{}` and absent identically, and a leftover `{}` makes the file look configured.\n- Keys the catalog doesn't know are read and written **verbatim** — upstream adds settings weekly, and silently hiding one would misreport the file.\n\n## Path guard\n\nAny path that isn't a Claude Code settings file is refused: must be absolute, named `settings.json` / `settings.local.json`, inside a `.claude/` directory. An admin endpoint that writes JSON anywhere on the box is a different and much larger thing than a settings editor.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **57 new tests.** The three critical guards were **mutation-tested** — reverting the presence-read rewrite, the empty-parent cleanup, and the re-read-before-write each turns tests red. They're guards, not tests that happen to pass.\n- **The masking test found a real leak during development**: the apply response echoed the plan, which carried the raw key in `after` while every other surface masked it. Masking now lives in `PlannedChange.as_dict()` so no consumer can reintroduce it.\n- **Live server**, throwaway home, port 8171: catalog served 518 entries; document masked a real key while leaving it intact on disk; plan wrote nothing; `DISABLE_TELEMETRY: \"0\"` removed the key; `FORCE_HYPERLINK: \"false\"` was rejected; apply wrote the file, took the backup, didn't echo the key; both path-guard probes returned 400. Server stopped, scratch removed, **WSL server on :8082 never touched** and still answering 200.\n- Full suite **3775 passed**, same 14 environment-baseline failures as an untouched worktree.\n- Wheel checked: `config/data/claude_code_config_catalog.json` ships.\n\nThe catalog moved from `docs/` into the package so there is **one copy** the page and the reference share.\n\nMINOR bump **5.7.2 → 5.8.0**.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TWCKNkSxNEfus8GfcqXnQD\n",
