    "message": "feat(admin): settings-editor API for the Configure Claude Code page\n\nThe page can write exactly two keys today, ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and\nANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN. Everything else about Claude Code -- model, effort,\npermissions, tool limits, telemetry, terminal behaviour -- has to be hand-edited\nin ~/.claude/settings.json. This is the backend for editing the rest.\n\nIt is built on the generated catalog from #114 rather than a hardcoded list, so\nthe surface it can edit tracks upstream instead of drifting the week after it\nlands. 518 entries, each carrying the control it wants: toggle, select with the\ndocumented option list, number, path, list, JSON, or secret.\n\nThree shapes make a naive settings editor do the OPPOSITE of what the user\nasked, so they are enforced in code rather than left to the UI:\n\n- Six variables are read for PRESENCE, not value. Writing \"0\" to\n  DISABLE_TELEMETRY leaves telemetry off. A request to set one to a falsey\n  value is rewritten into a key removal, with a warning saying why.\n- FORCE_HYPERLINK is parsed as a number, so \"false\" enables hyperlinks. Setting\n  it to a word is rejected outright, pointing at 0.\n- Ten variables carry credentials. Those are masked on the way out.\n\nWrites are two-stage. plan_changes touches no disk: it resolves each request\nagainst the catalog, records before/after, and attaches warnings. apply_plan\nwrites only what the plan said, after re-reading the file -- a plan the user\nreviewed for a minute must not clobber an edit Claude Code made meanwhile. A\nbackup is taken once, and the write is atomic via os.replace.\n\nTwo smaller correctness points, both with tests that fail without them:\nunsetting the last key under permissions removes the now-empty parent object,\nbecause Claude Code treats {} and absent identically and a leftover {} makes\nthe file look configured; and keys the catalog does not know are read and\nwritten verbatim rather than dropped, because upstream adds settings weekly and\nsilently hiding one would misreport the file.\n\nThe API refuses any path that is not a Claude Code settings file: absolute,\nnamed settings.json or settings.local.json, inside a .claude/ directory. An\nadmin endpoint that writes JSON anywhere on the box is a different and much\nlarger thing than a settings editor.\n\nFiles:\n- config/claude_code_catalog.py    typed loader over the packaged catalog\n- config/claude_config_editor.py   read / plan / apply, with the trap handling\n- api/admin_claude_config_routes.py  catalog, document, plan, apply\n- config/data/                     the catalog, moved out of docs/ so there is\n                                   one copy the page and the reference share\n\nVerification:\n- 57 new tests. The three critical guards were mutation-tested: reverting the\n  presence-read rewrite, the empty-parent cleanup, and the re-read-before-write\n  each turn tests red, so they are guards rather than tests that happen to pass.\n- The credential-masking test found a real leak during development: the apply\n  response echoed the plan, which carried the raw key in `after` while every\n  other surface masked it. Masking now lives in PlannedChange.as_dict() so no\n  consumer can reintroduce it.\n- Live server on a throwaway home, port 8171: catalog served 518 entries;\n  document masked a real key while leaving it intact on disk; plan wrote\n  nothing; setting DISABLE_TELEMETRY to \"0\" removed the key; FORCE_HYPERLINK\n  \"false\" was rejected; apply wrote the file, took the backup, and did not echo\n  the key; both path-guard probes returned 400. Server stopped and scratch\n  removed; the WSL server on 8082 was never touched and still answers 200.\n- Full suite: 3775 passed, same 14 environment-baseline failures as an\n  untouched worktree.\n- Wheel checked: config/data/claude_code_config_catalog.json ships.\n\nMINOR bump 5.7.2 -> 5.8.0: new capability, no behaviour change to anything\nexisting. No UI yet -- the page lands next.",
